# Book :1060 and P0: `name(value)` and `name: value` are one tree, so among f's actuals a frame whose head
# names a formal of f is that formal's argument, whatever else the name names.  Here g is both a method and
# f's formal: f(g(2)) gives f's g the value 2 -- 2 + 10, 12 -- not the result of the method g (which would
# give 30 + 10).  Entry 7.
fn: g (int: q) int
    return: q + 28
fn: f (int: g) int
    return: g + 10
int: r 0
r: f(g(2))
if: r != 12
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
